  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 General Election (November 3, 2026) (November 3, 2026)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Calendar\n\n Courts\n Elections\n\n Employment\n FAQ\n \n\n Translate Language\n \n Translate\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n Home\n \n\n Departments \n \n\n 911 Communications\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Community Services\n Conservation\n Emergency Management\n Engineer/Secondary Roads\n GIS\n Health & Sanitation\n Human Resources\n Information Technology\n Landfill & Recycling\n Planning & Development\n Recorder\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n Weed Commissioner\n \n \n \n\n About \n \n\n Cemeteries\n Elected Officials\n Township Information\n \n \n Apply\n Contact\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Clear · 46°\n \n \n\n Find departments, services, staff, and more\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nElections \n\n2026 General Election (November 3, 2026)\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \nNovember 3, 2026\n \nGeneral Election \n \n\n A General Election is the election in which federal and state officers, members of Congress and of the general assembly, county and township officers, and other officers appear on the ballot. General Elections are held the 1st Tuesday after the 1st Monday in November of each even-numbered year. \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Results Available on Election Night\n \n \n\n 0/15 Precincts Counted\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \nVoting Precincts\n \n\n Boone Ward 1\n \n\n Boone County Fairgrounds - Community Bldg. \n1601 Industrial Park Rd. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n Boone Ward 2\n \n\n Boone Open Bible Church \n1224 Hancock Dr. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n Boone Ward 3\n \n\n First Evangelical Free Church - Multipurpose Room \n1407 Kate Shelley Dr. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n Boone Ward 4\n \n\n Central Christian Church \n803 Greene St. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n Boone Ward 5\n \n\n Boone County Courthouse - First Floor \n201 State St. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n Madrid Ward 1\n \n\n Madrid Public Library \n100 W 3rd St. \nMadrid, IA 50156 \n \n\n \n \n\n Madrid Ward 2\n \n\n Madrid Public Library \n100 W 3rd St \nMadrid, IA 50156 \n \n\n \n \n\n Madrid Ward 3\n \n\n Madrid Public Library \n100 W 3rd St. \nMadrid, IA 50156 \n \n\n \n \n\n Ogden\n \n\n Leonard Good Community Center \n114 SW 8th St \nOgden, IA 50212 \n \n\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 1\n \n\n Central Iowa Expo - Administration Bldg. \n1827 217th Rd. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 2\n \n\n Luther Community Room \n7 Luther St. \nLuther, IA 50152 \n \n\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 3\n \n\n Woodward Resource Center (Bldg. 5, Chapel) \n164 Magnolia Dr., Bldg. 5 \nWoodward, IA 50276 \n \n\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 4\n \n\n Leonard Good Public Library \n208 W. Mulberry St. \nOgden, IA 50212 \n \n\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 5\n \n\n Leonard Good Community Center \n114 SW 8th St. \nOgden, IA 50212 \n \n\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 6\n \n\n Boone County Fairgrounds - Community Bldg. \n1601 Industrial Park Rd. \nBoone, IA 50036 \n \n\n \n \n\n\n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n Boone - 1st Ward \n \n \n\n Boone - 2nd Ward\n \n \n\n Boone - 3rd Ward\n \n \n\n Boone - 4th Ward\n \n \n\n Boone - 5th Ward\n \n \n\n Madrid - 1st Ward\n \n \n\n Madrid - 2nd Ward\n \n \n\n Madrid - 3rd Ward\n \n \n\n Ogden\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 1\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 2 \n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 2 - Madrid School District\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 3\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 3 - Madrid School District\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 4\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 5\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 5 - Pilot Mound Township\n \n \n\n Rural Precinct 6\n \n \n\n \nBack:\n Upcoming Elections \n\n \n \n\n \nResources & Services\n Drainage\n Elections & Voting\n Financial and Tax Information\n Real Estate\n FAQ\n Department Home\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nDid You Know\n \nSign up to receive notifications when board meetings and agendas are posted, job openings are announced, and more.\n Customize Your Notifications\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nMission Statement\n \nThe mission of Boone County is to be accountable to its citizens in providing innovative and high-quality\ngovernment services in an economical, fair, professional, and courteous manner to enhance and protect the\nhealth, welfare, and safety of those who live and work in Boone County.\n\n\n\n \nBoone County, Iowa\n\n 201 State St.\n\nBoone, IA 50036\n\n Contact Us\n \n\n \nCourthouse Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n\n 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\n\n Closed Holidays\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Boone County, Iowa\n \npowered by \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeteran’s Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving Day (November 26, 2026)\n \nBlack Friday (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve Afternoon (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas Day (December 25, 2026)\n \n\n\n\n\n\n"
